WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.046
A market adds a currency and an exchange rate for the shoppers of certain countries.

00:00:06.046 --> 00:00:10.251
This video shows why markets exist, how they fit together, and how to

00:00:10.251 --> 00:00:14.680
use every screen, from adding a market to the checkout with tax included.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.472
A shopper abroad who sees prices in a currency they do not use will often leave.

00:00:24.472 --> 00:00:27.490
They cannot tell what they would really pay.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:34.580
Pricing every product again for every country is a job that never ends, and rates move.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:39.328
A market adds a currency and an exchange rate for the shoppers of

00:00:39.328 --> 00:00:42.650
certain countries, and converts your prices for them.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.716
The shop, the cart, the checkout and the order all use the market's

00:00:47.716 --> 00:00:51.440
currency, and prices can include the tax shoppers expect.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.486
Your store has one currency of its own.

00:00:58.486 --> 00:01:03.610
A market adds another, with an exchange rate, for the countries you choose.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.264
A price you enter in the market's currency is used as it is.

00:01:08.264 --> 00:01:11.990
Any other price is converted at the rate, and rounded up.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:18.600
A market picker in the storefront lets shoppers choose their market, and the storefront remembers it.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:23.571
A product can be left out of a market, shipping can have prices

00:01:23.571 --> 00:01:28.160
in the market's currency, and a market can include tax in its prices.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.624
Open Commerce, Markets, and click Add market.

00:01:35.624 --> 00:01:40.090
Every shopper sees your store's own prices until you add a market.

00:01:40.672 --> 00:01:45.931
Enter a Name, such as Europe, which shoppers see in the market picker.

00:01:45.931 --> 00:01:51.466
Countries are two letter codes separated by commas, such as DE, FR and IT.

00:01:51.466 --> 00:01:54.372
A country can be in one market only.

00:01:54.825 --> 00:01:58.422
Enter the Currency, such as EUR, and the Exchange rate:

00:01:58.422 --> 00:02:02.845
how much of that currency one unit of your store's currency is worth.

00:02:02.845 --> 00:02:05.145
Your prices are multiplied by it.

00:02:05.602 --> 00:02:11.020
Price rounding rounds a converted price up, to the cent, to a whole

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.321
amount, or to .99 or .95.

00:02:13.321 --> 00:02:19.481
Prices include tax takes the tax out of the prices, and On offers the market.

00:02:19.481 --> 00:02:20.742
Click Save.

00:02:24.967 --> 00:02:29.145
When a market is on, the storefront's top bar shows a market picker.

00:02:29.145 --> 00:02:33.663
Click it, and Shop in lists your markets, and Everywhere else, which shows

00:02:33.663 --> 00:02:35.357
your store's own prices.

00:02:35.808 --> 00:02:37.036
Choose Europe.

00:02:37.036 --> 00:02:39.248
Every price switches to euros:

00:02:39.248 --> 00:02:42.688
converted at the rate, and rounded up by the rule.

00:02:42.688 --> 00:02:45.268
The storefront remembers the choice.

00:02:45.719 --> 00:02:47.663
Add a product to the cart.

00:02:47.663 --> 00:02:51.309
The cart, the checkout and the order are all in euros.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:58.373
Some products cannot be sold everywhere.

00:02:58.373 --> 00:03:02.753
On the product's editor, under Not sold in, tick the markets it is

00:03:02.753 --> 00:03:05.005
not sold in, and click Publish.

00:03:05.474 --> 00:03:10.122
Shoppers in that market still find the product in listings, but its card

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:14.354
says Not sold in, with the market's name, instead of Add to cart.

00:03:18.605 --> 00:03:21.368
Each shipping method has a Currency.

00:03:21.368 --> 00:03:24.985
Open Shipping, edit a zone, and click Add method.

00:03:26.084 --> 00:03:30.869
Choose Flat rate, name it, set its Currency to EUR, and enter an Amount.

00:03:30.869 --> 00:03:36.513
For a shopper in the market, methods in the market's currency are offered as they are.

00:03:36.513 --> 00:03:41.544
Without one, the methods in your store's currency are converted at the rate.

00:03:45.759 --> 00:03:51.379
At checkout, a shopper in Europe sees the order in euros, and shipping in euros too.

00:03:51.845 --> 00:03:55.964
With Prices include tax on, the tax from your tax rules is taken

00:03:55.964 --> 00:04:00.201
out of the price, and the order summary shows it as included, such

00:04:00.201 --> 00:04:01.614
as VAT 19 percent.

00:04:01.614 --> 00:04:04.085
The shopper pays the price they saw.

00:04:08.285 --> 00:04:12.638
A market can set a Language, which the storefront switches to, and the

00:04:12.638 --> 00:04:14.871
order's emails are written in it.

00:04:14.871 --> 00:04:17.505
The languages are your site's languages.

00:04:18.255 --> 00:04:22.978
Listing sorts and price filters work in your store's currency, and reports keep

00:04:22.978 --> 00:04:25.645
each order in the currency it was paid in.

00:04:26.395 --> 00:04:29.564
Exchange rates do not update by themselves.

00:04:29.564 --> 00:04:34.025
Check them now and then, and edit the market when a rate moves.

00:04:34.775 --> 00:04:37.875
The admin always shows your store's own prices.

00:04:42.075 --> 00:04:43.766
Selling in Europe:

00:04:43.766 --> 00:04:48.555
one market for several countries, in euros, with VAT included.

00:04:49.305 --> 00:04:51.138
A country of its own:

00:04:51.138 --> 00:04:55.685
a market for one country, with its own currency and rounding.

00:04:56.435 --> 00:04:57.760
Tidy prices:

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:03.205
round up to .99 or a whole amount so converted prices look intended.

00:05:03.955 --> 00:05:05.259
Restricted goods:

00:05:05.259 --> 00:05:08.945
leave a product out of the markets where it cannot be sold.

00:05:10.945 --> 00:05:17.152
Add a market, let shoppers pick it, and every price, cart and order follows their currency.

00:05:17.152 --> 00:05:18.815
Thanks for watching.

